// Rule 3: shell started by Apache (Sysmon for Linux)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Finding:        Commands sent to the web shell started a shell whose parent
//                 process was Apache.
// Data source:    Sysmon for Linux ProcessCreate events (HartwellSysmon_CL),
//                 Microsoft Sentinel.
// Time column:    OriginalTime (TimeGenerated is ingestion time in this data).
// Hunt window:    2026-10-23 04:00 to 16:00 UTC.
// Result:         62 hits for the web server account and 1 for root.
// What it missed: The first visit, because Sysmon only starts recording at
//                 05:24. The cron runs, because their parent is cron, not
//                 Apache. Rule 2 covers both.
// Expected false positives: The same as rule 2 (PHP features or plugins that
//                 shell out, such as image processing and mail; allow-list
//                 those commands by name).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
HartwellSysmon_CL
| where OriginalTime between (datetime(2026-10-23T04:00:00Z) .. datetime(2026-10-23T16:00:00Z))
| where RuleName == "ProcessCreate" and ParentImage == "/usr/sbin/apache2"
| where Image in ("/usr/bin/dash", "/bin/sh", "/usr/bin/bash", "/bin/bash")
| summarize Hits=count(), First=min(OriginalTime), Last=max(OriginalTime) by User
